        "Abstract": "The Cross-lingual Choice of Plausible Alternatives (XCOPA) is a typologically diverse multilingual dataset for causal commonsense reasoning. It is a translation and re-annotation of the English COPA and covers 11 languages from 11 different language families. We provide a detailed analysis of the dataset creation process, including the discussion of the main translation and cultural adaptation challenges. We use XCOPA to evaluate the zero-shot cross-lingual transfer capabilities of a range of massively multilingual transformers. We find that their performance substantially lags behind the monolingual performance of a comparable English model. The results suggest that XCOPA is a challenging benchmark for future research in cross-lingual transfer."
